#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:2
msgid "LDAP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:5
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:7
msgid ""
"The LDAP identity source authenticates users against an LDAP directory "
"and creates or updates the corresponding |morpheus| user at login. "
"Identity sources are configured per Tenant under |AdmTen| > selected "
"Tenant > :guilabel:`IDENTITY SOURCES`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:9
msgid ""
"Before configuring the source, obtain a directory URL, a least-privilege "
"bind account, the user distinguished-name (DN) pattern, user attribute "
"names, and the DNs of any groups used to restrict access or map Roles. "
"The appliance must be able to reach the directory endpoint. Use an "
"``ldaps://`` URL and a certificate issued for the directory hostname "
"whenever the directory supports TLS. Do not place production credentials "
"in examples, tickets, or screenshots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:12
msgid "Adding an LDAP Identity Source"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:14
msgid "Navigate to |AdmTen| and select a Tenant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:15
msgid ""
"Select :guilabel:`IDENTITY SOURCES`, then :guilabel:`+ ADD IDENTITY "
"SOURCE`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:16
msgid "Select ``LDAP`` and configure the following fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:18
msgid "URL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:19
msgid ""
"LDAP endpoint, including the scheme and port, for example "
"``ldaps://ldap.example.com:636``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:20
msgid "Binding Username"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:21
msgid ""
"DN or username for an account that can read the required users, "
"attributes, and groups."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:22
msgid "Binding Password"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:23
msgid "Password for the binding account. The value is stored as a secured field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:24
msgid "User DN Expression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:25
msgid ""
"Template used to construct the authenticating user's DN. ``$username`` is"
" replaced with the supplied login name, for example "
"``uid=$username,ou=people,dc=example,dc=com``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:26
msgid "Required Group DN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:27
msgid ""
"Optional group DN that a user must match before login is authorized. "
"Leaving it empty removes this group gate; successful directory "
"authentication can then create or synchronize a user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:28
msgid "LDAP Attribute Names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:29
msgid ""
"Attribute names used to read the username, common name, first name, last "
"name, email, group members, and user group memberships. The "
"implementation defaults to ``uid``, ``cn``, ``givenName``, ``sn``, "
"``mail``, ``uniqueMember``, and ``memberOf`` respectively when a value is"
" not supplied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:31
msgid ""
"Set the Default Role and map additional |morpheus| Roles to LDAP group "
"DNs. At login, group membership is tested against the configured user "
"membership attribute (and then ``uniqueMemberOf``). Each matching mapping"
" adds its Role; the Default Role is also assigned. With Manual Role "
"Assignment disabled, these identity-source Roles are recalculated on "
"login."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:32
msgid ""
"Save the source. Saving validates the URL, bind credentials, user DN "
"expression, Required Group DN, and mapped group DNs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:35
msgid "Testing and troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:37
msgid ""
"Test with a non-administrative directory user that is in the required and"
" mapped groups, then with a user outside the Required Group. Confirm the "
"resulting local profile attributes and Roles. If saving or login fails:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:39
msgid ""
"Verify DNS, routing, and the LDAP/LDAPS port from every appliance "
"application node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:40
msgid ""
"Verify the bind account can read the generated user DN and every "
"configured group DN."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:41
msgid ""
"Check that the User DN Expression produces the user's exact DN and that "
"attribute names match the directory schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:42
msgid ""
"Confirm group mapping values are full DNs and match the values returned "
"by the user's membership attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:43
msgid ""
"For LDAPS, verify the endpoint hostname and certificate chain. Do not "
"bypass certificate checks in external diagnostic clients or replace LDAPS"
" with clear-text LDAP as a production workaround."
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:45
msgid "Note"
msgstr ""

#: ../../integration_guides/IdentityManagement/ldap.rst:45
msgid ""
"The fields and defaults above describe the current LDAP implementation. "
"Directory schemas vary; use the attribute names and DN syntax returned by"
" your directory rather than assuming Active Directory conventions."
msgstr ""

